<worksheet xml:id="Catfish">
    <title>Catfish Population</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
           A chemical factory has set up business on a certain North Georgia river.  This river empties into a large lake, 
           on which is a restaurant which serves fresh catfish dinners. The chemical factory started dumping toxic waste 
           into the river, which reduced the catfish population. The table below shows how the number of catfish per acre 
           is related to the number of gallons of toxic waste dumped per day by the chemical factory.  Let <m>g</m> 
           represent the number of gallons of toxic waste dumped per day and <m>C(g)</m> represent the number of catfish 
           per acre. 
        </p>
        <tabular halign="center" bottom="minor" top="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
            <row>
                <cell>Gallons of toxic waste dumped per day</cell>
                <cell>5</cell>
                <cell>18</cell>
                <cell>23</cell>
                <cell>37</cell>
                <cell>48</cell>
                <cell>60</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
                <cell>Number of catfish per acre</cell>
                <cell>47</cell>
                <cell>40</cell>
                <cell>35</cell>
                <cell>30</cell>
                <cell>27</cell>
                <cell>19</cell>
            </row>
        </tabular>
    </introduction>
    <exercise>
        <p>
           Create a scatterplot of the data. <m>(g, C)</m>   (You do not need to copy this to your paper.) 
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="0.25in">
        <p>
            Using regression on Desmos determine a linear model to represent <m>C(g)</m>.
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="0.5in">
        <p>
          What are the "units" for the slope of this linear model?  
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="0.5in">
        <p>
          What meaning can we assign to the "<m>C</m>-intercept" of the model?  What is the value of the <m>C</m>-intercept?
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="0.5in">
        <p>
          What meaning can we assign to the "<m>g</m>-intercept" of the model?  What is the value of the <m>g</m>-intercept?
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="0.5in">
        <p>
         Find the value of <m>C(75)</m>.  Explain what it means in context of the problem.
        </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="0.5in">
        <p>
         Find <m>g</m> if <m>C(g)=60</m>. Explain what it means in context of the problem.
        </p>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>